BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Meet Your Classmates [REL C 333-033]
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260905
DTSTAMP:20260904T201600Z
UID:event-assignment-1441097
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:[] (https://byu.instructure.com/users/37820/files/1384509/prev
 iew?hidden=1&verifier=ttQHXneN6EqBJGmfx17gshSW3umPVhkIXJHKXVtO)You will cr
 eate a quick video so your class community can meet you. To begin\, introd
 uce yourself briefly to your classmates and instructor team—just your st
 andard getting-to-know-you information. Then answer at least three of the 
 following questions.\n\n* Tell about an experience you have had meeting or
  listening to a prophet or apostle.\n\n* What is one of your favorite talk
 s by a Church leader\, and why?\n\n* Share or ask something that might con
 nect you to some other classmates. (A shared major? Career goal? Mission l
 ocation? Hometown? Hobby?)\n\n* Share something that might set you apart f
 rom other classmates. (Maybe a unique skill or experience?)\n\n* When you 
 are not working or going to school\, what do you most like to spend time o
 n?\n\n* If you’ve taken an online semester course before\, do you have a
 ny advice or tips for your classmates?\n\nHere are [instructions to create
 /share a video] (https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/pages/resources
 -for-creating-videos). This is the first of several times that you'll subm
 it videos in this class\, so take a little time to figure out how it works
 . (It's often easiest to post a link to a video rather than try to upload 
 and embed.)\n\nAfter you submit your introduction video\, browse some of y
 our classmates' videos and respond thoughtfully to at least two of them (a
  text reply is fine). Remember that the goal is to create a sense of commu
 nity and a comfortable learning environment\, so you know . . . etiquette
 \, civility\, kindness\, and appropriate responses. Canvas discussions are
  laid out in an odd way\; they are in chronological order\, but the most r
 ecent posts are at the bottom of the page\, so for a large discussion like
  this\, maybe scroll down a ways to find some that haven’t been read or 
 commented on yet.\n\nYour initial video post is due by the indicated due d
 ate\, and you will have until the following week to post your two+ replies
  to other students. I invite you to check back and look at the discussion 
 to meet more classmates from your section and read any comments on your po
 st. You are welcome to comment on posts throughout the week\, even if you'
 ve already met the requirement. If you missed the first post deadline beca
 use you added the class on or after the first due date\, please type "Adde
 d late" at the beginning of your comment so that you won't be scored late.
 \n\nRubric: You will receive 3 points for your introduction video and 2 po
 ints for your replies to other students. Most thoughtful posts will receiv
 e full credit\, but if answers or replies are very brief or lack evidence 
 of genuine effort\, points will be reduced. To see the complete rubric\, c
 lick on the three dots in the top right corner of this page. Then click "S
 how Rubric."\n\nPhoto by [Naassom Azevedo] (https://unsplash.com/@naassom
 z1?utm_source=unsplash&utm_medium=referral&utm_content=creditCopyText) on
  [Unsplash] (https://unsplash.com/s/photos/college-students?utm_source=un
 splash&utm_medium=referral&utm_content=creditCopyText).
URL;VALUE=URI:https://byu.instructure.com/calendar?include_contexts=course
 _35044&month=09&year=2026#assignment_1441097
