 67" data-decorative="true" data-api-endpoint="https://byu.instructure.com/
 api/v1/users/37820/files/1384509" data-api-returntype="File" loading="lazy
 ">You will create a quick video so your class community can meet you. To b
 egin\, introduce yourself briefly to your classmates and instructor team
 —just your standard getting-to-know-you information. Then answer at leas
 t three of the following questions.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Tell about an experienc
 e you have had meeting or listening to a prophet or apostle.</li>\n<li>Wha
 t is one of your favorite talks by a Church leader\, and why?</li>\n<li>Sh
 are or ask something that might connect you to some other classmates. (A s
 hared major? Career goal? Mission location? Hometown? Hobby?)</li>\n<li>Sh
 are something that might set you apart from other classmates. (Maybe a uni
 que skill or experience?)</li>\n<li>When you are not working or going to s
 chool\, what do you most like to spend time on?</li>\n<li>If you’ve take
 n an online semester course before\, do you have any advice or tips for yo
 ur classmates?</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Here are <a title="Resources for Creating V
 ideos" href="https://byu.instructure.com/courses/35044/pages/resources-for
 -creating-videos" target="_blank" data-api-endpoint="https://byu.instructu
 re.com/api/v1/courses/35044/pages/resources-for-creating-videos" data-api-
 returntype="Page">instructions to create/share a video</a>. This is the fi
 rst of several times that you'll submit videos in this class\, so take a l
 ittle time to figure out how it works. (It's often easiest to post a link 
 to a video rather than try to upload and embed.)</p>\n<p>After you submit 
 your introduction video\, browse some of your classmates' videos and respo
 nd thoughtfully to at least two of them (a text reply is fine). Remember t
 hat the goal is to create a sense of community and a comfortable learning 
 environment\, so you know . . . etiquette\, civility\, kindness\, and appr
 opriate responses. <span style="background-color: #ffff99\;"><strong>Canva
 s discussions are laid out in an odd way\; they are in chronological order
 \, but the most recent posts are at the bottom of the page\, so for a larg
 e discussion like this\, maybe scroll down a ways to find some that haven
 ’t been read or commented on yet.</strong></span></p>\n<p>Your initial v
 ideo post is due by the indicated due date\, and you will have until the <
 em>following</em> week to post your two+ replies to other students. I invi
 te you to check back and look at the discussion to meet more classmates fr
 om your section and read any comments on your post. You are welcome to com
 ment on posts throughout the week\, even if you've already met the require
 ment. If you missed the first post deadline because you added the class on
  or after the first due date\, please type "Added late" at the beginning o
 f your comment so that you won't be scored late.</p>\n<p><strong>Rubric:</
 strong> You will receive 3 points for your introduction video and 2 points
  for your replies to other students. Most thoughtful posts will receive fu
 ll credit\, but if answers or replies are very brief or lack evidence of g
 enuine effort\, points will be reduced. To see the complete rubric\, click
  on the three dots in the top right corner of this page. Then click "Show 
 Rubric."</p>\n<p style="text-align: right\;"><span style="font-size: 8pt\;
 ">Photo by&nbsp\;<a href="https://unsplash.com/@naassomz1?utm_source=unspl
 ash&amp\;utm_medium=referral&amp\;utm_content=creditCopyText">Naassom Azev
 edo</a>&nbsp\;on&nbsp\;<a href="https://unsplash.com/s/photos/college-stud
 ents?utm_source=unsplash&amp\;utm_medium=referral&amp\;utm_content=creditC
 opyText">Unsplash</a>.</span></p><script src="https://instructure-uploads.
 s3.amazonaws.com/account_74070000000000001/attachments/8409019/dp_app.js">
